What was taken from them
------------------------
The network STRUCTURE: two 3x3 convolutions and the grid pool, a U-Net with
three down levels, a middle, three up levels with a nearest-neighbour
upsample and a skip concatenation, `features`, and the 1x1 `prob` (sigmoid)
and `dist` (linear) heads. `graph.py` implements that structure in our own
code, from `config.json` and the published architecture
(`csbdeep/internals/blocks.py:unet_block`, `stardist/models/model2d.py:_build`);
no source file of StarDist or CSBDeep was copied.

Not taken: their weight conversion, their normalisation, their tiling, their
NMS or their polygon code -- all of it is called as an installed package at
run time.

Weights
-------
`2D_versatile_fluo` (BSD 3-Clause per its model card) is converted once from
the installed `weights_best.h5` into a `.pt` file. The `.pt` is not part of
this repository and is not redistributed with it; see `envs/fusion_mesmer/models.json`
and `docs/v17_install_plan.md` for how each installation obtains the models.
